Description: Implements the closed-form rule for allocating detection effort
    across the levels of a nested survey at any depth. A nested survey is
    modeled as a cascade of conditional Bernoulli trials, with detection
    measured on a log (nat) scale so that the design problem separates into a
    chain of one-variable problems solved from the innermost level outward.
    The package computes optimal per-level replication under a budget or a
    required detection probability, serves both the detection and count goals,
    handles integer replicate counts, and extends to multiple targets and to
    multiple methods or places. Function and argument names mirror the
    equations of the accompanying manuscript.
